@ 2:5  A-|>>B: Hello
  2:4-2:7 "->>"
  | **`->>`** solid line, arrowhead: `A` → `B`
  |
  | `A->>B: text`: a message from `A` to `B`. `+` after the arrow activates `B`, `-` deactivates `A`; `()` on either side is a central connection.
@ 3:6  B--|>>A: Hi
  3:4-3:8 "-->>"
  | **`-->>`** dotted line, arrowhead: `B` → `A`
  |
  | `A->>B: text`: a message from `A` to `B`. `+` after the arrow activates `B`, `-` deactivates `A`; `()` on either side is a central connection.
@ 4:5  A-|xB: no
  4:4-4:6 "-x"
  | **`-x`** solid line, a cross at the end: `A` → `B`
  |
  | `A->>B: text`: a message from `A` to `B`. `+` after the arrow activates `B`, `-` deactivates `A`; `()` on either side is a central connection.
@ 5:5  A-||\B: half
  5:4-5:7 "-|\\"
  | **`-|\`** solid line, solid half arrowhead on the top: `A` → `B`
  |
  | `A->>B: text`: a message from `A` to `B`. `+` after the arrow activates `B`, `-` deactivates `A`; `()` on either side is a central connection.
@ 6:7  A->>|+B: on
  6:7-6:8 "+"
  | **`+`**
  |
  | `A->>+B`: activates `B`.
